* NOT PR MATERIAL -- kept as the record of a withdrawn investigation.
*
* Stock NitrOS-9 + the lost-update fix alone passes all eleven 6809 conformance
* tests. Neither hunk below could be shown to change any observable behaviour,
* and the EOF lock was never broken on 6809: stock already takes it for
* write-only producers and creators, and wakes waiters on every write. Do not
* apply this or send it upstream. See docs/nitros9-rbf-reference/README.md,
* section "2026-07-27 CONCLUSION".
*
--- a/level2/modules/rbf.asm
+++ b/level2/modules/rbf.asm
@@ -2228,12 +2228,21 @@
                     lbcs      L0AFF
                     ifgt      Level-1
                     pshs      u,y,x
+* Only a path open for update may take a RECORD lock.  A read cannot be
+* required to lock what it read unless the path is able to rewrite it, so a
+* read-only or execute-only path claims nothing here.  This gate covers the
+* record lock ONLY -- the eof lock at L0BF0 has a wider rule, see there.
+* Y is still the path descriptor here; L0BC2 restored U.
+                    lda       PD.MOD,y            get the open mode
+                    anda      #UPDAT.
+                    cmpa      #UPDAT.             both bits, not just one
+                    bne       LokNoRc             not update: claim nothing
                     ldy       PD.Exten,y
                     lda       #$01
                     lbsr      L0AD1
                     ora       PE.Lock,y
                     sta       PE.Lock,y
-                    clrb
+LokNoRc             clrb
                     puls      pc,u,y,x
                     else
                     clrb
@@ -2265,6 +2274,19 @@
                     cmpx      PD.SIZ+2,u
                     bcs       L0BF8
 L0BF0               equ       *
+* The EOF lock: "the end is not known yet, someone is still writing -- wait".
+* Any path that can WRITE may assert it, not only an update path: a plain
+* write-only sequential producer ('>') holds it exactly as an update one does,
+* which is what lets a read-only consumer follow a live writer instead of
+* mistaking the current end for the final end.  A read-only path asserts
+* nothing -- it can never extend the file, and a follower that locked the end
+* would block the very producer it is following.
+* U is the path descriptor here (L0BC2 did leau ,y before switching Y to the
+* extension).  A is dead on both arms: the 6809 arm reloads it below, and
+* L0BF8 enters with lda #EofLock.
+                    lda       PD.MOD,u            get the open mode
+                    bita      #WRITE.             can this path write at all?
+                    beq       L0C01               no: assert no eof lock
                     ifne      H6309
                     oim       #EofLock,PE.Lock,y
                     else
